    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d6f6284_ebca4c7d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-16T21:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We only need this for development, right? Maybe it\u0027s something that we only enable in local builds, but not in production builds.",
      "parentUuid": "6f83725d_211a3546",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0302e8be_59385c6a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-17T10:07:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I know we need this, but it makes me nervous from a security perspective.\n\nI see your point. It is basically a new potential attack vector. I\u0027m nervous as well.\n\n\u003e Can we design some sort of authentication mechanism or something along those lines?\n\nDo you have anything special in your mind? You mean something like integrity check via some magic number, not to accidentally enter bootloader or more like authentication e.g. with TA involvement? \n\n\u003e We only need this for development, right? Maybe it\u0027s something that we only enable in local builds, but not in production builds.\n\nThat is a problematic question. If we don\u0027t have that in mp builds, we just resign from the `flash_fp_mcu` script functionality, because there is no other method to force bootloader. Anyway, this CL adds possibility to include such command, guarded by the config.",
      "parentUuid": "1d6f6284_ebca4c7d",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4db95822_5b034170",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-20T20:31:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e not to accidentally enter bootloader or more like authentication e.g. with TA involvement?\n\nI was thinking about something that would prevent an attacker with root access from being able to send the \"enter bootloader\" command to the FPMCU. I think it would need to involve authentication with TA, but I haven\u0027t thought it through. IIRC, GSC has some protocol for enabling some development features. Maybe we could re-use that?\n\n@lziest@google.com, what are your thoughts? We don\u0027t have access to the bootloader code, so it\u0027s hard to audit.\n\n\u003e  we just resign from the flash_fp_mcu script functionality, because there is no other method to force bootloader\n\nIs there any restriction on entering the bootloader when we\u0027re in RW? If we can limit the command to only the RW image, then that gives us the ability to turn the command off in RW if there are some security issues.",
      "parentUuid": "0302e8be_59385c6a",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8c32c9d_f7291e23",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1505078
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-22T23:11:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I need to get educated first. Does this command require a pin to use? And once the ec enters the bootloader mode, it can stay in the bootloader mode and essentially can jump to any place?\n\nGenerally speaking, yes it will be nice if we can bind this potentially very-powerful-but-only-in-dev capability to the GSC dev mode. But I don\u0027t know how to do it, I will be happy to learn. Will apronin@ know some pointers?",
      "parentUuid": "4db95822_5b034170",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cd22d634_3e8b9469",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-24T09:52:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does this command require a pin to use?\n\nNo, we don\u0027t have additional pin in our connector with FPMCU.\n\n\u003e And once the ec enters the bootloader mode, it can stay in the bootloader mode and essentially can jump to any place?\n\nNo.\n\nGenerally, I think we need to trust the bootloader anyway. The SOC can stay in bootloader for other reasons that sending the HC e.g. if an integrity check fails (flash is corrupted for some reason), the bootloader won\u0027t jump to RO.",
      "parentUuid": "e8c32c9d_f7291e23",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3ab0545d_02152955",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-30T13:35:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you have any comment on this?",
      "parentUuid": "cd22d634_3e8b9469",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62c0ab48_8646ec01",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1505078
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T07:32:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Apologies for the late reply. As long as we don\u0027t allow applications to change bootloader I think I am ok with it. From the security angle, what is the worst case scenario? Does this increase some attackers\u0027 capability?",
      "parentUuid": "3ab0545d_02152955",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "deac4b5b_f6c4b48d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-05T13:06:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As long as we don\u0027t allow applications to change bootloader\n\nit is a hard requirement for SDCP.\n\n\u003e From the security angle, what is the worst case scenario? Does this increase some attackers\u0027 capability?\n\nA potential attack I see is that the attacker enters bootloader and the bootloader has somehow possibility to read RAM (templates, keys etc.) or entropy in Rollbacks.\n\nTo mitigate such threats, I\u0027m thinking about placing such command only in RO. It would allow us to erase entropy before jumping to bootloader and there shouldn\u0027t be any FP related content / secrets in RAM.\n\n@tomhughes@chromium.org @patrykd@google.com any thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "62c0ab48_8646ec01",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f1172d2_be02019b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-13T10:08:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I updated the CL to allow entering bootloader only if the system is unlocked. I think it is the safest option for now to proceed with the development.",
      "parentUuid": "deac4b5b_f6c4b48d",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d9ba21e_b27f018a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1441652
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-13T12:00:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My 2 cents:\n\n\u003e It would allow us to erase entropy before jumping to bootloader and there shouldn\u0027t be any FP related content / secrets in RAM.\n\nYeah, if the bootloader is able to read flash, then we will need to reset entropy before jumping to bootloader, so it won\u0027t make decrypting templates easier for attacker. There is also another thing: **are we sure that the entropy we are using currently was not read previously by the bootloader?** The only way we can know it is to reset entropy after we go back from \"dev\" mode to \"secure\" mode.\n\nI think, solving this issue is outside of the scope of this CL and using `system_is_locked()` here is the best thing we can do.",
      "parentUuid": "6f1172d2_be02019b",
      "revId": "ddb659b77b509f1784072da1a6becec4390e2789",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
